/-!
# Equivalence of categories of finite étale algebras for a Henselian pair

For a Henselian pair `(R, I)`, base change along `R → R ⧸ I` is an equivalence from the category
of finite étale `R`-algebras to the category of finite étale `(R ⧸ I)`-algebras
(`CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale.isEquivalence_baseChange_quotient`). In particular, for a Henselian local
ring `(R, 𝔪)`, base change to the residue field `R ⧸ 𝔪` is an equivalence on finite étale algebras
(`CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale.isEquivalence_baseChange_residueField`).

Full faithfulness holds more generally for `R`-algebra maps `A → B` from any étale `R`-algebra `A`
into any finitely generated projective `R`-algebra `B`
(`TauCeti.HenselianRing.comp_quotient_bijective`,
`TauCeti.HenselianRing.tensorProduct_map_bijective`): the Weil restriction
`WeilRestriction R B (B ⊗[R] A)` represents `T ↦ (A →ₐ[R] T ⊗[R] B)` and is étale over `R`, so its
`R`-points match its `(R ⧸ I)`-points by `TauCeti.HenselianRing.comp_bijective`.

For essential surjectivity
(`TauCeti.HenselianRing.exists_etale_and_finite_and_tensorProduct_algEquiv`), a finite étale
`(R ⧸ I)`-algebra `B₀` lifts along `R → R ⧸ I` to an étale `R`-algebra `A`
(`Algebra.Etale.exists_tensorProduct_algEquiv_of_surjective`). By the global form of Zariski's main
theorem, `A` agrees with a module-finite `R`-subalgebra `A'` on finitely many basic opens covering
`Spec A`. Finiteness of `A ⧸ IA` over `R` produces an element of `A'` congruent to `1` modulo `IA`
and lying in the ideal generated by those basic-open elements, which lifts via the universal coprime
factorization ring to an idempotent `e ∈ A'`; the clopen quotient `B = A ⧸ (1 - e)` is then finite
étale over `R` with `(R ⧸ I) ⊗[R] B ≃ₐ[R ⧸ I] B₀`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.HenselianRing.includeRight_comp_bijective`,
  `TauCeti.HenselianRing.comp_quotient_bijective`,
  `TauCeti.HenselianRing.tensorProduct_map_bijective`: for a Henselian pair `(R, I)`, an étale
  `R`-algebra `A`, and an `R`-algebra `B` that is finitely generated and projective as an
  `R`-module, reducing modulo `I` is bijective on algebra maps `A → B`.
* `TauCeti.HenselianRing.exists_etale_and_finite_and_tensorProduct_algEquiv`: every finite étale
  `(R ⧸ I)`-algebra is `(R ⧸ I)`-isomorphic to `(R ⧸ I) ⊗[R] B` for a finite étale `R`-algebra `B`.
* `CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale.baseChangeQuotientFullyFaithful`: `FiniteEtale.baseChange R (R ⧸ I)` is
  fully faithful.
* `CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale.isEquivalence_baseChange_quotient`: `FiniteEtale.baseChange R (R ⧸ I)`
  is an equivalence of categories.
* `CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale.isEquivalence_baseChange_residueField`: for a Henselian local ring `R`,
  `FiniteEtale.baseChange R (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R)` is an equivalence of categories.
* `CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale.baseChangeCompIso`,
  `CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale.isEquivalence_baseChange_of_bijective`: composition of `baseChange` in a
  scalar tower, and equivalence along bijective ring maps.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 15.13.2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09ZL)
* [A. Grothendieck, *Éléments de géométrie algébrique* IV₄, Proposition 18.5.15]
-/

